"""MAX messenger in large type, without a web browser.

PyMax (MIT, vendored in /usr/local/lib/b8k-max) speaks MAX's web protocol
over a WebSocket, as web.max.ru does, so no web engine is loaded: about
55 MB in all instead of a second browser. The first start shows a QR code
to scan in MAX on a phone; the session is then kept in
~/.local/share/b8k-max/web.db (mode 600). PyMax's simulated telemetry is
off: a person is typing here.

Pages: the chat list (initials, name, last message, time, unread count)
and a chat (bubbles, photos, a large entry and a send button). New
messages arrive live and buzz. PyMax runs in its own thread with an
asyncio loop; every call from the window goes through run(), every answer
comes back with GLib.idle_add.

It lives in the background: b8k-launcher starts it with --background at
session start, closing the window only hides it, and the panel's MAX
button brings the same process back (one instance through D-Bus). The
unread count of dialogs and groups (channels left out) goes to
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/b8k-badge/max, which b8k-launch shows on the button, and
the panel is told at once (SIGRTMIN+7). Chats open from a cache: the last
messages of each chat on disk (~/.cache/b8k-max/chats, mode 600) and the
last six chats kept built in memory; only newer messages are fetched.
"""
